@startuml CAP_Graceful_Degradation
!theme plain

title CAP Protocol - Graceful Degradation

participant "Full Host" as FH
participant "Minimal Server" as MS

note over FH
  Host declares all capabilities:
  create_node: true
  invoke: true
  roots: true
  notifications: true
end note

note over MS
  Server declares minimal:
  sync: true
  immediate_call: false
  push_dirty: false
  push_notifications: false
end note

FH -> MS : initialize(host_capabilities: {all true})
MS --> FH : InitializeResult(server_capabilities: {minimal})

note over FH
  Host adapts behavior:
  - Does NOT send node/call
  - Does NOT expect node/dirty
  - Polls via node/sync on every tick
  - Server never pushes
end note

== Polling Mode (no push notifications) ==

FH -> MS : node/sync(node_id, calls=[])
note right : Poll for state changes\nsince server can't push
MS --> FH : NodeSyncResult(state, renders, ...)

FH -> MS : node/sync(node_id, calls=[{method: "cancel"}])
MS --> FH : NodeSyncResult(state, renders, ...)

== What Host Must NOT Do ==

FH -[#red]x MS : <color:red>node/call (BLOCKED)</color>
note over FH, MS : immediate_call: false

== Interoperability Guarantee ==

note over FH, MS
  Implementations at different conformance levels
  MUST interoperate at the **intersection** of
  their capabilities via capability negotiation.
end note

@enduml
